  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tCapium 365\n\t\tCapium 365 (Accountant)\n\n### Capium 365: Manage Imports (Users)\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Wed, 8 Oct, 2025 at  7:00 PM\n\n\t\tWithin the Capium 365 Manage Imports section, the import of clients, users, and templates helps you bring in the data efficiently. \n\nClick here to go to the Manage Imports page. \n\nImport of Users \n\nUsers can be imported using the sample file method: \n\n1. Navigate to the Imports section. \n\n2. Select User as the type to import and press Next. \n\n3. Download the User sample file. \n\n4. Enter the required user information. \n\n5. Upload the completed file into the system. \n\nOnce the file is uploaded, Capium 365 will automatically verify the data. After successful verification, the details of the clients will be displayed within the system.\n\nBelow are some articles that we recommend following next for a seamless set-up in Capium 365:\n\nAdding users in Capium 365 (via My Admin)Capium 365: Manage Imports (Clients)\n\nCapium 365: Inviting your client to join\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
